# Expenses source map (`expenses/src`)

Go straight here instead of wandering the GitHub Pages dump at repo root.

| Need | Place |
|---|---|
| Types | `types/types.ts` (`TransactionOrIncomeItem`, `AuthState`, `DataItems`) |
| Categories, API URL | `utils/constants.ts` (`ROOT_URL`) |
| Routes (`/expenses/...`) | `config/routes.ts` + `App.tsx` |
| Global state | `context/` — `useData`, `useAuthState`, `dataDispatch`; actions in `context/actions.ts` |
| Derived totals | `utils/dataProcessing.ts` + `dataProcessor.worker.ts` (don't recompute in the page) |
| Offline / API | `utils/offlineAPI.ts`, `indexedDB.ts`, `syncService.ts` |
| UI primitives | `components/ui/` (`StatCard`, `Modal`, `NumberDisplay`, `Notification`) |
| Feature UI | `components/{transactions,income,charts,layout,privacy,ai,budgets,sync,profile}/` |
| Pages | `pages/{Home,Charts,Income,AddTransaction,Profile,Login,Assistant}/` |
| Styles | **`App.scss` only** — CSS vars (`--accent-color`, `--bg-color`, `--surface-*`). No new CSS files, no CSS-in-JS |
| Crypto / lock | `crypto/` + `components/privacy/` |
| In-app AI | `ai/` — keys must not go in `VITE_*` |

**Speed:** match naming and file placement next to neighbors; reuse `StatCard` / `Modal` / filters; add SCSS under the existing page/component section; don't add Redux/Zustand/Tailwind/MUI. `yarn start` on :3000, `yarn build` to check.
